      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Camera calibration round-trip: calibrate -> save -> load -> undistort\n\nLEFT branch: six synthetic chessboard photos (different angles, with lens distortion baked in) are batched and fed to 'Calibrate Camera (Chessboard)', which recovers the camera matrix + distortion coefficients. 'CV Save Camera Params (JSON)' writes them to output/demo_camera_params.json.\n\nRIGHT branch: 'CV Load Camera Params (JSON)' reads that file back and cv2.undistort straightens a distorted board with it.\n\nFIRST RUN reads the seeded demo_camera_params.json (Save hasn't overwritten it yet, and Load's dropdown is built when the page loads). RELOAD the page and run again to undistort with the params THIS graph just calibrated - the true round-trip.\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
